  "result": "Perfect! All 169 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support to invoices:\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM.\"\n\n**Added to src/dates.js:**\n\n1. **lastDayOfMonth(date)** \u2014 Returns last day of the month\n   - Takes YYYY-MM-DD date\n   - Returns last day as YYYY-MM-DD\n   - Handles leap years correctly\n\n2. **calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)** \u2014 Calculates due date based on terms\n   - Supports 'NET14' (14 days from issue date)\n   - Supports 'NET30' (30 days from issue date)\n   - Supports 'EOM' (end of issue date's month)\n   - Returns null for unknown terms\n\n**Updated createInvoice in src/invoices.js:**\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Validates terms (rejects unknown terms with TERMS_INVALID)\n- Calculates dueDate using calculateDueDate\n- Stores both `terms` and `dueDate` on the invoice object\n- Invoice now includes: customerId, issueDate, dueDate, terms, status, lines\n\n**Added 20 new tests:**\n- 9 tests for createInvoice with various terms\n- 11 tests for date calculation functions (lastDayOfMonth, calculateDueDate)\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- NET14: 14 days after issue (e.g., issued 2026-10-07 \u2192 due 2026-10-21)\n- NET30: 30 days after issue (e.g., issued 2026-10-07 \u2192 due 2026-11-06)\n- EOM: Last day of issue month (e.g., issued 2026-10-07 \u2192 due 2026-10-31)\n- All calculations in UTC\n- Handles month/year boundaries correctly\n- Leap year aware\n\nAll 169 tests passing.",
